 ### [ROI-Level Quantitative Evaluation](18860-roi-level-quantitative-evaluation.md)
-ROI-Level Quantitative Evaluation assesses the reconstruction quality of specific, semantically important regions within a rendered volume or image, rather than evaluating the entire scene uniformly. It addresses the limitation of global metrics by isolating local features—such as vegetation crowns, structural details, or fine surface textures—to verify visibility and fidelity where they matter most. It differs from full-image assessment by focusing on representative target features and from global target-focused evaluation by applying standard perceptual metrics within fixed spatial windows rather than aggregating over logical object masks. [Link to child article](18860-roi-level-quantitative-evaluation.md)
